parameters: max_frequency=224 few_apex_worst=18 max_k14=6 max_multiplier=180
[0] Assumption challenge / quotient declaration
  considered vertices:
    runners, gaps, fixed sections, section boundaries, wall-crossing events,
    residues, cover arcs, lift packets, Fourier modes, and proof obligations.
  chosen vertices:
    Fourier bands 1-7, 8-14, 15-28, 29-56, 57-112, 113-224.
  LRC predicate preserved:
    positive strict Haar mass is the L2 mass of 1_U, and a positive
    Fejer convolution against 1_U is a spectral witness of nonempty U.
  information destroyed:
    endpoint-owner labels, C27 shell addresses, and exact packet family.
  challenged assumption:
    that the proof must locate a local boundary pinch.  This route asks
    whether every live packet has a finite trigonometric shadow, or else
    a high-frequency tail controlled by relation-lattice structure.

